35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Whoa! One bill for everyone means no one gets stuck paying extra! That’s so much fairer than last time.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The 8,000 yen gap last year was unacceptable. A single bill for the whole house eliminates that uncertainty entirely.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that last year we barely saw each other, yet the shared house left no room for quiet. I need a place that balances both.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The ferry eats two full days. The train takes ninety minutes. I need to know which option preserves the most actual holiday time.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found the inn has one shared bathroom and fixed meal times. The city room has a door and no schedule.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, two days lost to the ferry sounds awful! I hope the train is much faster so we can actually play!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, the ninety-minute train is far more efficient. It preserves the week, which is what matters.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, the train saves us two days. That means more time for us to actually be together, which is what I need.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Sakura, the train is ninety minutes. The ferry takes two days. I need the week back, not spent waiting.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Midori, the fixed meal times worry me. I need to know if I can eat when I’m hungry, not when the clock says.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that sounds tough! But maybe the island house is better? I found out it’s one big bill, so nobody pays extra!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the city room offers a door and no timetable. That flexibility might help you sleep better than a shared schedule.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Daisuke, I hear you. The shared house left no room for quiet, but the city offers a door. I hope that privacy helps you rest.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the city trains run every few minutes. You can move without waiting for a bus that stops early.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, a door and no timetable sounds much better. I worry about the cold water and fixed meals at the inn.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I’m so happy the island house means one fair bill! No more guessing who pays what. That feels really safe and fun for all of us!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"The single bill resolves the 8,000 yen discrepancy. I need certainty on the total cost before we commit. The island option offers that clarity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
